# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Multi-Currency Wallet -- environment template
#
# Copy this file and fill in only what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. This file is committed, so it must never hold a
# real URL or token.
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT. Copy the file, change
# nothing, and `npm run dev` / `npm test` still work -- with no Redis set the
# app uses an in-memory ledger that needs no credentials. The variables matter
# when you deploy, or when you want to exercise the Redis path locally.
#
# The only place these are read is src/infrastructure/container.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Ledger storage: Upstash Redis over HTTP -------------------------------
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION, optional locally.
#
# Why Redis at all: a serverless host gives no instance affinity, so a ledger
# held in process memory loses writes between requests -- a reviewer would make
# a deposit and watch it vanish. Redis makes the store shared, so any instance
# reads the same ledger.
#
# Two naming schemes are accepted for the same service, because the two ways of
# provisioning it set different variable names. Set ONE pair, not both.
#
# Pair 1 -- Vercel Marketplace / Vercel Storage (checked first).
# Injected automatically once an Upstash store is connected to the project, so
# on Vercel you normally never type these by hand. Set them here only to point
# local development at the same store.
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://<your-store>.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=<rest-token-from-the-upstash-dashboard>
#
# Pair 2 -- a direct Upstash account (used when pair 1 is absent).
# From the Upstash console: your database -> REST API -> "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_*".
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<your-store>.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=<rest-token-from-the-upstash-dashboard>
#
# Note the protocol: the adapter speaks Upstash's HTTP REST API, not the Redis
# wire protocol. A local `redis-server` or a plain `redis` Docker container
# cannot stand in for it -- it does not speak HTTP. Use a free Upstash store, or
# leave these unset and develop against the in-memory ledger.


# --- Set by the platform, never by you -------------------------------------
#
# VERCEL is set to "1" inside any Vercel build and runtime. The app uses it to
# decide that a missing Redis configuration is fatal rather than something to
# quietly fall back from: on Vercel with no Redis, startup throws. Do not set
# this locally -- doing so makes local development refuse to start for the
# same reason.
# VERCEL=1


# --- Deploy-time only: not read by the application -------------------------
#
# Needed only to deploy from the command line with `npx vercel`. The dashboard
# Git integration needs none of this -- it is the simpler path and the one the
# README recommends.
#
# Create at https://vercel.com/account/tokens
# VERCEL_TOKEN=<personal-access-token>
#
# Only needed for non-interactive CI deploys, where there is no `.vercel`
# directory to read the linkage from. `npx vercel link` writes them for you.
# VERCEL_ORG_ID=<team-or-user-id>
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=<project-id>
